	"summary": {
		"text": "The Bassa of central Nigeria speak Basa, a Kainji language, in several varieties: Basa-Komo (Kwomu) in Kogi and Nasarawa, and Basa-Kwali, Basa-Gurara and Basa-Makurdi elsewhere. They live in the FCT, where Gwagwalada is their traditional headquarters, and in Kogi, Nasarawa and Benue. Bassa speakers often also speak Igala, Ebira or Nupe. They are not the same people as the Bassa-Nge.",
